From bb62828cf080786a2cffa54d9f89943b3b461ec3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Mills <96480787+josephomills@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 02:25:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support modified_beam_search with hotwords for streaming NeMo
 transducer models (#3895)

A hypothesis that emitted max_symbols_per_frame tokens on one frame is
advanced to the next frame without decoding a blank. The counter was
incremented there, so a frame that emitted ten symbols was reported as one
frame of silence. The greedy decoder leaves the counter alone in this case:
it is zeroed by each emitted token and incremented only by a decoded blank.

The over-report is bounded to one frame, since the next emission resets the
counter, but it is visible to endpointing right after a saturated frame.
Measured on a 6.6 s clip with --blank-penalty=20, which saturates the cap on
every frame: greedy reports 0 trailing blanks, this decoder reported 1 before
the change and 0 after. Normal decoding (penalty 0) is byte-identical before
and after.
